<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CCITTModifiedHuffman> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One-dimensional CCITT T.4 run-length coding of bilevel rows without EOL codes, each row starting on a byte (rowAlignment 8, TIFF compression 2) or 16-bit word (rowAlignment 16, TIFF compression 32771) boundary, decoded with libtiff's recovery rules. Output: rows of ceil(columns / 8) bytes, most significant bit first, 1 for black."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CCITTModifiedHuffman> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CCITTModifiedHuffman> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CCITT Modified Huffman"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CCITTModifiedHuffman> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CodecScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The controlled concept scheme grouping codec values. Membership identifies the applicable value set; raw format codes are defined by profiles rather than by this scheme."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#CodecScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
